= FLA conditions get more stringent

With public debt reaching past the 35% of GDP mark, continued financing through the FLA, the central-government-run liquidity fund, comes under "enhanced" fiscal supervision. In plain language, this translates to enforced austerity measures and more supervision over Catalan public spending until the financial situation is reverted back to a more "acceptable" state. Needless to say, this also lowers the Generalitat's credibility in other financial markets, making debt seeking even harder.

- @post_event: This is really not great...
